{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403047-campaigns-with-limited-knowledge","id":1403047,"title":"Campaigns With Limited Knowledge","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-15T23:15:44-07:00","id":1403047,"title":"Campaigns With Limited Knowledge","content":"My mythological knowledge goes to a fairly limited few pantheons. I know the most about Greek and Norse and I am fairly proficient with Egyptian. However, there are a lot of them out there. Even in the core book, there is a cornucopia to choose from. And some of those may appeal to players. Has anyone tried to do it with only a handful (or less) for starting off with? If so, did you include more as time went on?<br /> <br /> Now, one solution is to read up on the Pantheons but that means tons of homework in addition to prepping a game and running the game on top of other things like work/school/responsibilities.<br /> <br /> Anyone got any ideas on how to handle this situation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T00:09:12-07:00","id":1403054,"title":"","content":"When I started Scion, I didn't know too many pantheons either. Japanese, Greek and Nordic were those I was most familiar with, the others I learned with time. Usually by preparing story hooks that referenced the appropriate mythology in one way or another. Just because you don't know a lot of some of the myths doesn't mean you cannot use them. :-) <br /> <br /> If you feel uncomfortable with giving players access to pantheons you yourself do not understand to the appropriate degree, theres no shame in limiting their choices until more open up. I did this too and the game became even richer for it. Maybe there is an alliance between some pantheons, maybe the players are even all descended from one Pantheon for story reasons. Personally, I would limit my players choices, which doesn't have to be restrictive, until I feel comfortable with more mythologies to give into their hands. Just remember that time is your friend here and you are not running a sprint, but a marathon. Pick up small bits and pieces here and there. Watch a documentary, visit a museum, read a book, but don't try to learn everything there is to learn. The great thing about myths and Scion is that a lot of things are still open for interpretation and can certainly be viewed from a lot of different perspectives. And most of all, enjoy!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","name":"Asmael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T10:10:12-07:00","id":1403111,"title":"","content":"You can always cut some pantheons out of your game, in fact it\u2019s better than portrait them poorly or have a players questioning the way you are portraying a god that they chose to put into your game.<br /> <br /> My suggestion is following one of the options Ars Magica gave about historical games:<br /> - Research as much as possible what ever you are going to put on your game (maybe keep a few Wikipedia entrances ready to go if required)<br /> - Get only what you can and keep distance from the rest;<br /> - It\u2019s your game you play however you prefer.<br /> <br /> of course they wrote better in the book, but it\u2019s your game, so talk to the players and chose the approach you prefer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T05:20:49-07:00","id":1403210,"title":"","content":"Start off with the pantheons you know really well and use the others when you have time to research them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T10:28:02-07:00","id":1403247,"title":"","content":"As I do <a href=\"https://geekandsundry.com/roleplaying-basics-the-importance-of-session-zero/\" target=\"_blank\"><b><i>Session Zero</i></b></a> - or, rather <i>Month Zero,</i> or even <i>Half Year Zero</i> ( <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) - I ask players in the poll about Pantheons. As I prepare 'serious' RPG chronicles for about months, even half year before, I got time. Mostly, before those kind of game, I do private Facebook group or small Discord server - and start there topics for players to easily answer in the free time. Their answer shape game and I have time to research what I need in mean time. Chosen main Pantheons point to general starting location of the game - with pointing cross <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1278657-pantheons-conflicts-regions\">Pantheons Conflicts Regions</a></b>.<br /> <br /> <b>Note: </b>As I play myself as SG, I also marks my options in poll - I prefer Aesir, Theoi and Bogi - but I still open for learning new Pantheons. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Note 2: </b>I generally run two chronicles at the same time - one 'serious' and one 'light-hearted' - to not go with Game Master burn out. When I'm preparing 'serious', I run 'light-hearted' in meantime, hashing sensible and trustworthy players for future 'serious' one. 'Light' game of my choosing is, most often, <b>Monarchies of Mau</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Here is the simple poll I do from Pantheons from <b>Scion</b> 2E corebooks - I ask players each their 3 favorite or interesting - and we go from then on. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u2022 Aesir - Nordic Gods,<br /> \u2022 Bogi - Slavic Gods, ( I'm Slavic enthusiast )<br /> \u2022 Deva - Gods of India (in Asia),<br /> \u2022 Kami - Japanese gods,<br /> \u2022 Manitou - Gods of the Algonquin People,<br /> \u2022 Netjet - Egyptian gods,<br /> \u2022 Orisha - Gods of Yoruba (Africans),<br /> \u2022 Shen - Chinese Gods,<br /> \u2022 Theoi - Greek-Romanesque Gods,<br /> \u2022 Tuatha De Danann - Gods of the Celts,<br /> \u2022 Teotel - Gods of the Aztecs","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-18-2020, 04:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T11:21:01-07:00","id":1403254,"title":"","content":"Honestly in my case I just told my players I know little more about a number of these pantheons than is written in the book. So, if any of them happen to know more on a subject for one that is likely to come up, and if one of them is a Scion of that pantheon assume good odds it will, and would get offended by me running it as more than just an extrapolation of behavior as explained in the book they should probably fill me in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T23:40:30-07:00","id":1403347,"title":"","content":"My ultimate dodge is using the Gods as little as I need, TBH. I'm blessed with a group of players who really enjoy character-focused narratives. Bring in themes if you can find them, bring in some motifs, maybe mirror some stories if you want, but ultimately I like to run my sessions where the story is about <i>the Heroes</i>.<br /> <br /> That said, if you feel uncomfortable with certain things because you don't feel like you can do them justice, there's no shame at all in admitting it to your players. Session Zero <i>is</i> very important, both to lay some groundwork and to plan out what kinds of stories you want to tell. During this point, it's easy to go &quot;I know fuck all about the Orisha so if you'd like to play an Orisha Scion I may need to do additional research&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Manitou - Gods of the Algonquin Indians</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit I'm not from one of those tribes but AFAIK they'd prefer to be called something like &quot;The Algonquin People&quot; or &quot;Algonquin Nations&quot; rather than 'Indians'. Indians is kind of a disrespectful way to refer to them. IIRC you're not from the Americas so I can understand not knowing this, just for future reference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tuatha de Danann - Gods of the Celts </div> </div> </div>Ireland, specifically. A 'Gods of the Celts' would be smashing like several dozen different tribal groups together and going &quot;They're all the same anyway&quot;. Scion refers to the Gods of the various Gaulish tribes as the Nemetondevos, while the Gods of Wales will be the Plant Don. Saying a figure is from 'Celtic Myth' is about as helpful as saying that a word is from 'A Romantic Language', which may not be incorrect persay but isn't really telling the whole thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T04:45:07-07:00","id":1403365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403047-campaigns-with-limited-knowledge?p=1403347#post1403347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My ultimate dodge is using the Gods as little as I need, TBH. I'm blessed with a group of players who really enjoy character-focused narratives. Bring in themes if you can find them, bring in some motifs, maybe mirror some stories if you want, but ultimately I like to run my sessions where the story is about <i>the Heroes</i>.<br /> <br /> That said, if you feel uncomfortable with certain things because you don't feel like you can do them justice, there's no shame at all in admitting it to your players. Session Zero <i>is</i> very important, both to lay some groundwork and to plan out what kinds of stories you want to tell. During this point, it's easy to go &amp;quot;I know fuck all about the Orisha so if you'd like to play an Orisha Scion I may need to do additional research&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> I admit I'm not from one of those tribes but AFAIK they'd prefer to be called something like &amp;quot;The Algonquin People&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;Algonquin Nations&amp;quot; rather than 'Indians'. Indians is kind of a disrespectful way to refer to them. IIRC you're not from the Americas so I can understand not knowing this, just for future reference.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ireland, specifically. A 'Gods of the Celts' would be smashing like several dozen different tribal groups together and going &amp;quot;They're all the same anyway&amp;quot;. Scion refers to the Gods of the various Gaulish tribes as the Nemetondevos, while the Gods of Wales will be the Plant Don. Saying a figure is from 'Celtic Myth' is about as helpful as saying that a word is from 'A Romantic Language', which may not be incorrect persay but isn't really telling the whole thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will they be doing a Welsh pantheon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T05:16:46-07:00","id":1403373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403047-campaigns-with-limited-knowledge?p=1403365#post1403365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Will they be doing a Welsh pantheon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hopefully. They have mentioned it in the Companion, in the Nemtondevos section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T07:03:38-07:00","id":1403383,"title":"","content":"Awesome \ud83d\ude0a\ud83d\ude0a\ud83d\ude0a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T07:40:48-07:00","id":1403389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403047-campaigns-with-limited-knowledge#post1403047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My mythological knowledge goes to a fairly limited few pantheons. I know the most about Greek and Norse and I am fairly proficient with Egyptian. However, there are a lot of them out there. Even in the core book, there is a cornucopia to choose from. And some of those may appeal to players. Has anyone tried to do it with only a handful (or less) for starting off with? If so, did you include more as time went on?<br /> <br /> Now, one solution is to read up on the Pantheons but that means tons of homework in addition to prepping a game and running the game on top of other things like work/school/responsibilities.<br /> <br /> Anyone got any ideas on how to handle this situation?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is nothing wrong with doing a game with just two or three Pantheons surviving in the modern time. Do what you feel most prepared for and what you think will be the more interesting story. You can always trickle in revelations of a wider world later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T11:25:07-07:00","id":1403404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403047-campaigns-with-limited-knowledge?p=1403365#post1403365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will they be doing a Welsh pantheon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hopefully. I keep making references to them in the Scion books; they'll eventually have to give in. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Scion 2E</b> Freelancer: <i>Origin; Hero; Demigod; God; Mythical Denizens; Mysteries of the World; Saints &amp; Monsters; No Gods, No Masters; Once &amp; Future, Realms of Magic &amp; Mystery</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/369-geoffrey","name":"Geoffrey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T12:21:31-07:00","id":1403408,"title":"","content":"Yeah, to clarify, they haven't OFFICIALLY announced a Welsh Pantheon writeup but I know Geoffrey would love nothing more.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, for the OP, even if you go with All The Pantheons Exist (which I do), nothing stops you from going &quot;But for this story we're going to focus on these five-&quot; for the sake of a campaign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 07-18-2020, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T19:02:34-07:00","id":1403459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403047-campaigns-with-limited-knowledge?p=1403408#post1403408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, to clarify, they haven't OFFICIALLY announced a Welsh Pantheon writeup but I know Geoffrey would love nothing more.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, for the OP, even if you go with All The Pantheons Exist (which I do), nothing stops you from going &amp;quot;But for this story we're going to focus on these five-&amp;quot; for the sake of a campaign.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I ever ran Scion, I would also rule that all the pantheons exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T01:39:05-07:00","id":1403498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403047-campaigns-with-limited-knowledge?p=1403459#post1403459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I ever ran Scion, I would also rule that all the pantheons exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean that's a good deal of the fun, isn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T01:48:07-07:00","id":1403499,"title":"","content":"That is a supported playstyle. The Companion has it (the number of pantheons and other myths important to the game) listed as on it's dials.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T16:33:40-07:00","id":1403589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1403047-campaigns-with-limited-knowledge?p=1403498#post1403498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean that's a good deal of the fun, isn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]}]}